TC07 - Verify Documentation Version Switcher

Test Steps
Step	Action	Expected Result
1	Open https://playwright.dev/docs/intro	Installation documentation page is displayed successfully.
2	Locate the version dropdown/selector (e.g., displaying "Next" or current version number).	Version selector is visible on the page.
3	Click the version dropdown.	A list of available versions (e.g., "Next", previous stable versions) is displayed.
4	Select an older version from the list.	Page navigates to the documentation for the selected version.
5	Verify the current URL reflects the selected version (e.g., contains a version number/path segment).	URL updates to match the selected version.
6	Verify a version banner/notice is displayed indicating this is not the latest version.	An outdated-version notice/banner is visible on the page.
7	Click the link/button to return to the latest version.	Page navigates back to the current/latest documentation version.

Expected Final Result
The user can successfully switch between different documentation versions, confirm the version-specific URL and banner are correct, and return to the latest version.